  'In Addition & Condensation Polymers, when an ideal gas undergoes reversible isothermal expansion at temperature $T = 500\text{ K}$ from volume $V_1 = 1\text{ L}$ to $V_2 = 6\text{ L}$, the change in internal energy $\Delta U$ is:', 'For an ideal gas, internal energy depends solely on temperature: $U = f(T)$. Since the process is isothermal ($\Delta T = 0$), $\Delta U = n C_v \Delta T = 0$.',
