  'Evaluating the limit in LHospitals Rule: $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin(2x)}{\tan(3x)}$ is equal to:', 'Using standard limit properties: $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin(ax)}{\tan(bx)} = \lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\frac{\sin(ax)}{ax} \cdot ax}{\frac{\tan(bx)}{bx} \cdot bx} = \frac{a}{b} = \frac{2}{3}$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE ADVANCED-2020-MATH-Q11', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
