  'e193fb73-b804-4aca-a822-2323bb0d4f2b', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', '754cf45c-0d59-4879-a1a0-a73723ee7903', 'f355858d-ea5e-4162-a614-d15ee63c7591',
  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in 1D Motion such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 528t^2 - 1056t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(528)t - 1056$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 1056\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2013-PHY-Q19', 'APPROVED', TRUE
