  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'ADVANCED',
  'In an electric circuit analyzing Vector Algebra, a parallel plate capacitor of capacitance $C = 10\ \mu\text{F}$ is connected across a potential difference of $V = 20\text{ V}$. The energy stored in the capacitor is:', 'Energy stored in a capacitor is given by $U = \frac{1}{2} C V^2$. Substituting $C$ and $V$ yields the required stored electrostatic energy.',
