  '90bfea0d-0d6b-4f05-a1fe-370284a85a7b', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', 'c64f775f-ece4-4e6d-ac17-240f89ff14e7', 'b86ffe90-fd71-447c-afd0-3a357d6ceced',
  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'MEDIUM',
  'In Continuity Criteria, the value of the definite integral $\int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3(x)}{\sin^3(x) + \cos^3(x)} dx$ is:', 'Applying King''s property $\int_a^b f(x) dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x) dx$, let $I = \int_0^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^n x}{\sin^n x + \cos^n x} dx$. Adding both equations gives $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'NEET-2024-MATH-Q30', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
