  'JEE_ADVANCED', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Photoelectric Effect such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 1096t^2 - 2192t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 3$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(1096)t - 2192$. Substituting $t = 3$, we obtain $a = 4384\text{ m/s}^2$.',
