  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Moment of Inertia such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 1464t^2 - 2928t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(1464)t - 2928$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 2928\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2019-PHY-Q25', 'APPROVED', TRUE
