  'A particle moves along a straight line in Refraction at Spherical Surfaces such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 1620t^2 - 3240t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(1620)t - 3240$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 3240\text{ m/s}^2$.',
