  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Moment of Inertia such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 1860t^2 - 3720t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(1860)t - 3720$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 3720\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2010-PHY-Q1', 'APPROVED', TRUE
