  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in 1D Motion such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 2112t^2 - 4224t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(2112)t - 4224$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 4224\text{ m/s}^2$.',
