  'fdd682a2-51c3-467c-a7b5-ad5f92d0c64d', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', '4bcf925f-6876-4f0d-ae61-c3c89a456425', 'f09e832d-6504-4f4a-a0bd-036302d650cb',
  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'MEDIUM',
  'In Properties of Determinants, the value of the definite integral $\int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3(x)}{\sin^3(x) + \cos^3(x)} dx$ is:', 'Applying King''s property $\int_a^b f(x) dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x) dx$, let $I = \int_0^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^n x}{\sin^n x + \cos^n x} dx$. Adding both equations gives $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2019-MATH-Q10', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
