  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in First Law of Thermo such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 2660t^2 - 5320t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 4$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(2660)t - 5320$. Substituting $t = 4$, we obtain $a = 15960\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'NEET-2015-PHY-Q21', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
