  'A particle moves along a straight line in Faradays Law & Lenz such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 2936t^2 - 5872t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 4$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(2936)t - 5872$. Substituting $t = 4$, we obtain $a = 17616\text{ m/s}^2$.',
