  'JEE_ADVANCED', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Photoelectric Effect such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 3076t^2 - 6152t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 3$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(3076)t - 6152$. Substituting $t = 3$, we obtain $a = 12304\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE ADVANCED-2011-PHY-Q17', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
