  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Faradays Law & Lenz such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 3332t^2 - 6664t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 4$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(3332)t - 6664$. Substituting $t = 4$, we obtain $a = 19992\text{ m/s}^2$.',
