  'JEE_ADVANCED', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'MEDIUM',
  'In Roots of Unity, the value of the definite integral $\int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3(x)}{\sin^3(x) + \cos^3(x)} dx$ is:', 'Applying King''s property $\int_a^b f(x) dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x) dx$, let $I = \int_0^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^n x}{\sin^n x + \cos^n x} dx$. Adding both equations gives $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE ADVANCED-2014-MATH-Q20', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
