  'For a reaction involving Adsorption Isotherms, the rate constant is $k = 4.5 \times 10^{-3}\ \text{s}^{-1}$. The order of this chemical reaction is:', 'The unit of rate constant is $\text{s}^{-1}$ which uniquely corresponds to a first-order reaction since $\text{unit} = (\text{mol}/\text{L})^{1-n} \text{s}^{-1} \implies 1-n = 0 \implies n = 1$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2016-CHEM-Q7', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
