  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'HARD',
  'A wheel of radius $R = 0.3\text{ m}$ is undergoing Angular Momentum. If its angular speed increases uniformly from $\omega_0 = 10\text{ rad/s}$ to $\omega = 50\text{ rad/s}$ in $t = 5\text{ s}$, the angular acceleration $\alpha$ is:', 'Using rotational kinematics $\omega = \omega_0 + \alpha t \implies \alpha = \frac{\omega - \omega_0}{t} = \frac{50 - 10}{5} = 8.0\text{ rad/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'NEET-2015-PHY-Q21', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
