  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in First Law of Thermo such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 3848t^2 - 7696t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 4$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(3848)t - 7696$. Substituting $t = 4$, we obtain $a = 23088\text{ m/s}^2$.',
