  'fdb4d748-4622-4a59-ab2c-22772ff66bc4', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 'cd7db698-ab4b-4009-af70-ca45115a75ac', 'd1ad2b71-d4f0-40c7-a2dc-6b57356418be',
  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'ADVANCED',
  'In an electric circuit analyzing AC Transformers, a parallel plate capacitor of capacitance $C = 14\ \mu\text{F}$ is connected across a potential difference of $V = 10\text{ V}$. The energy stored in the capacitor is:', 'Energy stored in a capacitor is given by $U = \frac{1}{2} C V^2$. Substituting $C$ and $V$ yields the required stored electrostatic energy.',
