  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'A particle moves along a straight line in Refraction at Spherical Surfaces such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 3996t^2 - 7992t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 2$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(3996)t - 7992$. Substituting $t = 2$, we obtain $a = 7992\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2016-PHY-Q7', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
