  'e34800d0-170c-4331-a5a5-6ce01523de62', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000003', 'de73e2fe-224b-447a-ad56-0d2eae35072c', '2c07eae6-8d06-4006-a881-5f20264d2a33',
  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'MEDIUM',
  'In Linear Differential Equations, the value of the definite integral $\int_{0}^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^3(x)}{\sin^3(x) + \cos^3(x)} dx$ is:', 'Applying King''s property $\int_a^b f(x) dx = \int_a^b f(a+b-x) dx$, let $I = \int_0^{\pi/2} \frac{\sin^n x}{\sin^n x + \cos^n x} dx$. Adding both equations gives $2I = \int_0^{\pi/2} 1 dx = \frac{\pi}{2} \implies I = \frac{\pi}{4}$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'NEET-2021-MATH-Q12', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
