  'JEE_ADVANCED', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'HARD',
  'For a square matrix $A$ of order $3$ in Inverse Function Properties, if $\det(A) = 6$, then the value of $\det(2A)$ is:', 'For an $n \times n$ matrix, $\det(k A) = k^n \det(A)$. For order $n=3$, $\det(2A) = 2^3 \det(A) = 8 \times 6 = 48$.',
