  'NEET', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'For a reaction involving Stoichiometry, the rate constant is $k = 9 \times 10^{-3}\ \text{s}^{-1}$. The order of this chemical reaction is:', 'The unit of rate constant is $\text{s}^{-1}$ which uniquely corresponds to a first-order reaction since $\text{unit} = (\text{mol}/\text{L})^{1-n} \text{s}^{-1} \implies 1-n = 0 \implies n = 1$.',
