  'ea196b5d-2a06-4b2c-acec-2ca1b1c6994a', '11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'fd3629b1-d688-4729-a91b-c6588d1d7e0c', '24fd880f-8ee4-46b1-a921-6034e5ba9458',
  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'EASY',
  'For a reaction involving Adsorption Isotherms, the rate constant is $k = 9 \times 10^{-3}\ \text{s}^{-1}$. The order of this chemical reaction is:', 'The unit of rate constant is $\text{s}^{-1}$ which uniquely corresponds to a first-order reaction since $\text{unit} = (\text{mol}/\text{L})^{1-n} \text{s}^{-1} \implies 1-n = 0 \implies n = 1$.',
