  'A particle moves along a straight line in Photoelectric Effect such that its velocity is given by $v(t) = 4924t^2 - 9848t + 3$ m/s. What is its acceleration at $t = 3$ seconds?', 'Differentiating velocity with respect to time: $a(t) = \frac{dv}{dt} = 2(4924)t - 9848$. Substituting $t = 3$, we obtain $a = 19696\text{ m/s}^2$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE ADVANCED-2014-PHY-Q5', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
