  'JEE_MAIN', 'SINGLE_MCQ', 'HARD',
  'In Diazonium Salts, when an ideal gas undergoes reversible isothermal expansion at temperature $T = 500\text{ K}$ from volume $V_1 = 1\text{ L}$ to $V_2 = 4\text{ L}$, the change in internal energy $\Delta U$ is:', 'For an ideal gas, internal energy depends solely on temperature: $U = f(T)$. Since the process is isothermal ($\Delta T = 0$), $\Delta U = n C_v \Delta T = 0$.',
  'PREVIOUS_YEAR', 'JEE MAIN-2022-CHEM-Q13', 'APPROVED', TRUE
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
